iats, an FARDC border garrison, ANR and border services, and the villages fall under PNC posts, territorial administration and customary chiefs. Insecurity consists of ordinary crime, smuggling and occasional cross-border spillover from CAR (refugee inflows, armed individuals crossing), which does not amount to territorial control by another actor. Web search was unavailable in this run (search budget exhausted, Wikipedia blocked), so the assessment rests on default state presence and general knowledge."}}